	// composition sees it; by class name, because a scoped rule cannot otherwise reach another
	// component's markup. Astro compiles TwinUnit's own rules to `:where()`, which scores zero, so
	// these win on specificity alone.
	//
	// What it buys: the unit's name matches the twin's name, and its device rows match the twin's
	// keys — same size, same weight, same line height. It shipped a step larger and a step heavier
	// on both, which read as two different cards rather than two views of one object. The name also
	// leaves $font-weight-semibold behind, which has no real face and was being synthesised.
	.tc :global(.unit__name) {
		font-size: u(16);
		font-weight: $font-weight-medium;
		line-height: u(22);
	}

	// Size and line height matched to the twin's rows, but the MEDIUM weight kept: these sit on the
